# Project Title: Cesar Cypher

This code is used to decypher or encode a message for someone as was done in the time of Cesar the emporer.

## Description

In ancient rome, Cesar would send his generals encrypted messages where the you would need to know something called a "shift number". This means that every character in the message was shifted by a certain number which would only be known by allies or high level executives.

This code aims to mimic the cesar decoding and encoding method to encode a message using a shift number that will be known by the user alone.


### Dependencies

optional: art.py - this script has the logo for the game. Not mandatory but adds a little bit of flavour to the mix.

### Installations Needed

NA

